# ICA-Based Coexpression Module Analysis

**Identify signed gene modules from expression data using independent component analysis and expression-coherence refinement.**

## Overview

The supplied R script runs `picaplot::runICA()` on a log-transformed expression matrix, assigns genes to the positive or negative tail of their dominant component, and refines these modules using gene–module correlations (`kME`). Each gene is assigned to at most one final module; genes failing the criteria remain `Unassigned`.

This workflow identifies modules and their expression profiles. It does not calculate a gene–gene adjacency matrix, export a network edge list, or perform module–trait association tests.

