The diagnostic PDF includes an activity heatmap scaled by component. It is a display transformation, separate from the exported activity values. The supplied code does not guard the heatmap call against a result with fewer than two components; check the log if plotting fails after the tables have been written.

## 7. Downstream use

| Question | Appropriate result |
| :--- | :--- |
| Which genes form a retained module? | `Final_Module` and the per-module gene tables |
| How does an ICA component vary across samples? | Component activity table |
| How does a particular signed gene set vary across samples? | Signed-module PC1 table |
| Are modules associated with traits, eQTLs or genomic intervals? | Additional analyses using module profiles or gene sets |
| Which gene pairs form network edges? | Additional gene–gene association calculations; no edge table is generated here |

`IC1_pos` and `IC1_neg` originate from the same component and should not be counted as two independent ICA components. Component-level association should use one activity profile per IC. Signed-module PC1 profiles summarize different retained gene sets and are calculated separately.

